I
R
I</b>

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>NOBORIBETSU</b>

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.380
<i>At the time, Noboribetsu was 
Hokkaido's largest hot springs area.</i>

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.020
<i>The springs there had healing properties,</i>

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.170
<i>and after the Sino-Japanese War
 and Russo-Japanese War,</i>

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.370
<i>the 7th Division would send 
their sick and wounded.</i>

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.880
<b>Noboribetsu's Famous
"Burning Waterfall"</b>

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.650
I feel so good!

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.980
I'm reborn!

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.470
Privates Nikaido and Usami...

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.720
Did you just get here today?

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.850
Warrant Officer Kikuta.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.700
How is your recuperation going?

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:54.740
Oh, did Lieutenant Tsurumi send you because 
he was worried about how I was doing?

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.490
He must be looking forward to how much 
stronger his army will be after my arrival.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.380
By the way, did you hear that strange 
story Private Ariko was telling?

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:10.750
What did he say?

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:16.880
Last night, he met a strange man in 
a hot spring further up the mountain.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.910
The man was running through the snow,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:22.090
at night, carrying no light 
and wearing geta sandals.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.800
Strange, yes?

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.490
My left ball is changing 
places with my right ball!

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:15.690
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:03.550
<b>Episode Thirty-Nine
The Smell of Sulfur</b>

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.030
A man wearing geta sandals 
on a dark, snowy mountain?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.650
Well, there are snow geta 
you can wear in winter.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:13.320
And if he was running in the dark, perhaps 
his eyes were simply used to the darkness.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:18.440
What's so strange about that? Sheesh...

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.250
Anyway, busy now!

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.860
He can tell you himself.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.330
Right, Private Ariko?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:31.490
I heard the sound of geta, but the 
footprints on the ground weren't from geta.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.940
They were from straw boots.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.390
And so? Why is this so important to you?

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.070
There was more to the story, right, Ariko?

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:44.340
The clothes he wore were... curious.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.590
The pattern on them was unusual.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:47.830
Like how?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.890
I couldn't really say, 
because it was so dark...

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.120
You two have been here 
since the end of the war.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.590
The hot springs have scrambled your brains.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.090
Now, now, Nikaido.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:10.100
What were you doing at a hot spring that 
far up in the mountains, Private Ariko?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.560
It's a secret hot springs 
that only the Ainu know about.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.690
You an Ainu?

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:16.940
Yes.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.840
Perhaps he's an Ainu, too?

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.060
And the strange patterns on his 
clothes were an Ainu pattern.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.070
I would recognize an Ainu pattern.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:29.600
Something about this story 
seemed really strange to me.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.430
Am I just thinking about it too much?

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:33.190
You know anything, Mister Masseur?

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:36.790
Clothing with strange Ainu patterns?

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.610
I'll tell you if I see any.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.800
That's funny!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.020
No way! How?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.530
Come on, help me out, Nikaido.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:10.670
Tell me what the tattoos on the prisoners 
who escaped from Abashiri looked like.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.410
Never seen one.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.740
Let's go eat.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:28.430
Ariko, go ask at your village if anyone 
else has seen this strange man.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.800
Understood.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.310
We're in a bad spot because 
of Usami and Nikaido.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.560
Those assholes don't believe us.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:40.230
If we want to go back to serving under 
Lieutenant Tsurumi, we'd want to bring a gift.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:47.070
Are we taking Warrant Officer Kikuta 
and Private Ariko back to Abashiri?

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.840
No, Lieutenant Tsurumi
is leaving Abashiri soon.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:52.450
We'll meet up with him somewhere.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:56.670
What about the fortune-teller 
and the old cannibal?

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.170
Will he bring them?

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.390
That's not my problem.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.940
Hey, would you please stop 
punching me like that?

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:10.180
Massage me carefully. It hurts!

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.290
You suck at this.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.890
Oh, sorry.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:22.040
Those two that just arrived 
were with Lieutenant Tsurumi.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.770
They're a valuable source of information.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:28.220
We should get rid of the soldiers 
named Ariko and Kikuta before they

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.410
realize who we are.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.510
We should wait for the next new moon.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:35.290
The moonlight off the snow 
makes the winter nights bright.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.110
We need to hurry.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.220
If we have to leave, 
we'll cease to be able to

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:44.040
give information about the 7th 
Division to Hijikata Toshizou.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:48.090
Toni-san, you're the one who 
let that soldier see you.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.510
This is your mess to deal with.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:01.690
<i>The hot springs he spoke of, further up
 the mountain than Noboribetsu,</i>

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.520
<i>is currently known as 
the Karurusu Hot Springs.</i>

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:07.990
<i>The local Ainu called them "penke-yu."</i>

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:15.160
Am I going to see the geta 
man tonight, I wonder?

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:26.820
Have you seen a man wearing clothes with 
a strange pattern around penke-yu lately?

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:30.440
Someone who comes to bathe at dusk.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.810
<i>The sound of geta!</i>

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.700
Those aren't clothes.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.580
They were tattoos.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.510
<i>This is the man Ariko spoke of.</i>

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.890
<i>He has a light with him, but...</i>

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.630
You there. Take off your 
jacket and let me see you.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.640
<i>He can see me?</i>

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:23.390
<i>I had a light with me to stop his 
eyes from adjusting to the darkness!</i>

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.940
<i>He has friends with him?</i>

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.200
I can see all of you.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:41.060
<i>According to one theory,</i>

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.910
<i>pirates wore eyepatches so that when they 
needed to charge below the decks of a ship,</i>

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.420
<i>they could quickly adjust to the darkness.</i>

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.870
<i>Warrant Officer Kikuta</i>

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:55.270
<i>anticipated a night battle, and had
worn an eyepatch since sunset.</i>

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.680
<i>He could see in the dim darkness just fine!</i>

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.380
Retreat! He can see you!

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:05.890
That's why I told you to do it 
on the night of the new moon!

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.270
That's not good.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:12.110
Go! Go! Get into the valley!

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.050
You ain't getting away.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.540
I can't see a thing.

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.760
<i>I'm sick of the smell of sulfur.</i>

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.270
<i>Once I get my share of the gold, 
maybe I'll move to the coast.</i>

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.360
Got him!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.750
You got him!

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:10.250
That's in the direction of Hell Valley.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:19.590
Don't scratch my guns, shithead. 
I won these fair and square!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.810
<i>During the Russo-Japanese War,</i>

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:25.570
<i>Warrant Officer Kikuta became 
obsessed with stealing handguns</i>

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:28.100
<i>from the Russia officers he killed.</i>

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:32.360
<i>The Nagant M1895 was a personal favorite,</i>

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.350
<i>so much that he had his 
men search for them as well.</i>

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:45.240
Don't shoot! It's me!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.750
There are more with him!

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:54.670
<i>This is going like shit!</i>

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.930
He fled into the mountains!

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:03.310
Warrant Officer Kikuta!

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:05.370
Ariko, is that you?

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:09.060
What I saw was a tattoo.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.140
We'll follow him. After me.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:19.070
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:27.290
Usami, you asshole. Your timing 
was a little too convenient.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:31.580
You and Nikaido were actually staking 
out the Ainu hot springs, weren't you?

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:35.790
Let me guess: the two of you figured out 
what was going on from Ariko's story,

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.050
and were planning on 
finding the man before us.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.880
Whoops. Guess you figured it out.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.560
Why would a tattooed prisoner

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:53.270
take the risk of hiding at a hot springs 
filled with members of the 7th?

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.020
Oh, I've seen him.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.350
He's a masseur.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:17.210
His footsteps lead inside.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:21.010
It's an old mine tunnel. I went 
inside once when I was a kid.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.420
Any other exits?

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.970
Several, if they haven't collapsed.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.470
It's coming from further inside.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.430
Don't light any matches.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.730
It'll make you a target.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.410
<i>I can't see a thing.</i>

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.520
<i>What's this?</i>

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.130
<i>There's something on the ground.</i>

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:03.170
<i>If we're not careful,
we'll give away our location.</i>

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.390
<i>The ice stalagmites created by 
water dripping to the ground</i>

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:11.010
<i>and freezing are called hyoujun, 
or "ice bamboo shoots."</i>

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:14.890
<i>Even in Hokkaido, they can 
only be seen in a few places.</i>

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.100
Now it's my turn.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:22.390
<i>Looks like the prisoner has 
particularly good ears.</i>

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:28.740
<i>He's using the sound of the 
ice breaking to target us.</i>

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:34.330
<i>I never even noticed the ice 
when I came here before.</i>

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:37.500
<i>If I had a cinoyetat I could avoid them,</i>

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:41.500
<i>but a light like that would 
make me an easy target.</i>

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.370
Bastard!

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:06.570
<i>He's moving fast, but I don't 
hear any shattering ice.</i>

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:11.450
<i>How is he able to dodge it in this darkness?</i>

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.470
<i>And even with the volcanic gases at 
Hell Valley, he and his buddies...</i>

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.310
<i>A torch?</i>

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.930
He's a masseur!

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:51.320
He'd never seen us to begin with.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:54.330
They found me! Now things are bad!

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:55.990
A masseur?

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:59.080
He's using sound to get an accurate 
picture of his surroundings.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.350
There's probably some secret 
to that sound of geta sandals,

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.590
but it doesn't matter.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.970
So he ran outside?

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:20.390
Warrant Officer Kikuta, 
I was shot in the leg!

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.200
Please don't leave me here!

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.320
It's dark!

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.820
He's so damn annoying.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.820
Let me go alone.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.900
I've got an idea.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.700
A hunt is best done silently and alone.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.250
Fine.

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:38.200
Don't let him get away.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.960
I need to get the bullet out...

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.470
Should we really let Ariko go on his own?

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.280
Stop talking.

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:02.660
You're in no position to question anybody.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:07.870
And Ariko was part of the 
Mt. Hakkoda search party.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:12.770
<i>The Lost March of Mt. Hakkoda!</i>

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.000
<i>Two years before the Russo-Japanese War,</i>

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.350
<i>Aomori's 5th Infantry Regiment</i>

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.810
<i>was doing a march in the snow 
as part of winter training.</i>

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.860
<i>During this march 199 men lost their lives,</i>

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:26.460
<i>in what was one of the worst 
mountaineering accidents in history.</i>

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:31.460
He was one of the Ainu brought from Hokkaido?

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:35.530
The Ainu search parties walked 
through waist-deep freezing water,

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:38.770
and moved across deep snowy mountains 
like they were open plains.

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:41.350
They found the bodies and brought them back.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.680
Even the locals were astonished.

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:47.170
And he knows this mountain 
like his own backyard.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:51.900
Escaping from Ariko Rikimatsu on 
this mountain... is impossible.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:17.470
There's something about those 
breaking branches I don't trust.

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:43.230
<i>What is this sound?</i>

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:51.390
<i>So that's it...</i>

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.200
<i>He led me right where he wanted me,</i>

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:57.630
<i>to a place where this could easily happen.</i>

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.260
I lose.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.030
<b>Four Days Later</b>

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.290
Where's Warrant Officer Kikuta?

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.410
He went to the mountains to search again.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:30.040
It's been four days and Private Ariko 
isn't back. He's probably dead.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.100
Did you send a telegram to Lieutenant Tsurumi?

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:33.920
Yeah.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:37.130
He says he's coming here.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.120
Ariko's dead, and I injured my leg,

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.230
and we let the prisoner get away.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:47.140
He'll scold me again!

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.650
Ipopte...

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:03.070
Hey, Ariko. If you're alive, say so.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.370
I was worried.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:06.200
I've been waiting for you.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.950
Why did you strip off his skin?
 Explain, Ariko.

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:19.790
When I checked the tattoos, I realized that 
they stopped at the body's medial line.

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.380
At the medial line?

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:26.230
It was an instruction to strip off 
the skin like you would an animal's.

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:27.140
I see.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:32.600
It was too deep in the mountains for 
me to easily be able to carry it back.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.400
So I stripped it off there.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:40.050
And there was a chance that Usami 
and Nikaido would steal our prize.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:45.660
So I hid here in the village 
until you came to look for me.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:49.920
And his gun?

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.410
I assumed you'd want it, so I looked for it.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.410
But it was buried in the avalanche.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:58.420
The only prizes I brought 
back are his skin, and this.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.510
Well done, Ariko.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.550
You made the right call every time.

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:06.430
This is the perfect gift 
for Lieutenant Tsurumi.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:11.680
Now we can get back the time we wasted.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.940
Whatcha making, Granny?

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:24.700
I hope it's something 
that goes well with sake!

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.270
Rice soaked in water?

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:28.700
What are you doing with that?

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:44.720
<i>It's unknown if it's a 
Karafuto Ainu tradition,</i>

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.970
<i>but there is a record of a dish 
called "Grandma-Chewed Dumplings."</i>

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.620
<i>The grandchildren said,</i>

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:55.230
<i>"It was delicious! It was delicious, 
and that's all there is to it!"</i>

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:14.000
It's like the kiritanpo we have in Akita, 
made by crushing and baking leftover rice.

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.450
Hey! Hey!

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:19.320
Give me more of granny's dumplings!

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.200
Pirka, pirka.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:24.370
Make us more, Granny!

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:25.860
Okay?

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.260
Pirka, pirka.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:30.260
I can't wait anymore, Granny!

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.970
Put them right into my mouth!

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:36.770
<i>What the hell is wrong with these two?</i>

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:42.050
Tsukishima...

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:43.400
Yes?

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:48.270
What does bar... "barchonak" mean in Russian?

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:49.930
Barchonok?

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:54.360
It's what you'd say to make 
fun of a noble's son.

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:57.620
In other words, a spoiled rich kid.

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:00.040
Where did you hear that?

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Spoiled Rich Kid</b>

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:38.510
<i>Next time: "Spoiled Rich Kid"!</i>
